  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COUNCIL OF EUROPE ACTION PLAN FOR UKRAINE 2018-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Council of Europe&#x2019;s Action Plan for Ukraine 2018-2022 is a strategic programming instrument which accompanies Ukraine in its efforts to bring legislation, institutions and practice further into line with European standards in the areas of human rights, the rule of law and democracy. This supports Ukraine in meeting its obligations as a Council of Europe member State. Reforms aim to combat corruption, protect prisoners&#x2019; rights, increase access to legal aid, protect the human rights of Internally Displaced Persons, protect minorities, improve media independence and the safety of journalists, promote gender equality and enhance Civil Society&#x2019;s role in the reform processes.</narrative>
  </description>
